{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790291214,"nonce":"oXX21F5XUkL9h35Lxb+U/1fNj2A=","title":"Lua typer: a table constructor's computed number key does not type the element it stores","message":"A table constructor entry `[e] = v` whose key is a number not known at compile time (`{[one] = 5}`, `{[2] = 7}` read through a variable) does not join v into the shape's element type. The element stays Unknown, reads under a number key are then typed nil, and `t[i] == nil` and `t[i] or 0` fold to the nil answer while `print(t[i])` still finds the value.\n\n    local one = 1\n    local t = {[one] = 5}\n    print(t[1], t[one] == nil, (t[1] or 0) + 1)   -- lua5.4: 5 false 6; zylua: 5 true 1\n    local u = {[2] = 7}\n    local i = 2\n    print(u[i], u[i] == nil)                       -- lua5.4: 7 false; zylua: 7 true\n\nReproduces on main 678f49eb (NUC, both tiers). The constructor path needs to feed the entry through the same store rule as `t[k] = v` (element for a number key, dyn_value and every named field for a key that may be a string).","files":null}]}